    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** (74.86) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) anchor the Austin Waves lineup as our strongest plays. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite combination of high-order placement and a favorable matchup against Freddy Peralta; specifically, Peralta\u2019s slower delivery provides a slight boost to **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s aggressive base-running upside in a category that remains our scarcest priority. Meanwhile, **Jacob Wilson** faces a high-floor matchup against Cody Bradford (xERA 5.29). Despite the \"Lineup Pending\" tag, we are banking on his favorable park factor and high skill-based projections to anchor the MI slot. **Jackson Merrill** also provides elite value (69.72) from the #5 spot, as the dynamic platoon advantage against Bibee elevates him well above his base projection.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the marginal utility of **Coby Mayo** (42.34) versus our active OF/UTIL cohort. While **Coby Mayo** represents a high-upside bat, the optimizer ultimately pivoted away from him due to a lower projected batting average contribution and a suboptimal #8 spot in the order against a tough arm in Peralta. We also remain cautious with **Kyle Tucker** (51.57); while he is a cornerstone player, his score is currently suppressed by a difficult matchup against Logan Henderson and his pending status in the #6 hole. **Luis Robert Jr.** (51.97) remains in the lineup despite a dynamic platoon disadvantage because of the potential for stolen bases against a pitcher with a slow delivery profile\u2014a tactical necessity for us given the league\u2019s 5x5 constraints.\n\nWe are monitoring the status of **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** closely, as both remain \"Lineup Pending.\" Should either be scratched, we will look to re-evaluate our bench depth, though we remain without the services of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** due to his ongoing IL stint. With **Drake Baldwin** and **Sam Antonacci** providing reliable table-setting production at the top of the order, our priority remains maximizing speed-category efficiency. We are comfortable keeping **Wade Meckler** (42.06) on the bench today, as his platoon disadvantage against lefty Noah Cameron prevents him from cracking a saturated outfield rotation.",
